  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q19-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "$f(x)=x^2-1$ and $g(x)=4x+5$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q19-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "For this part only, restrict the domain of $f$ to $x\\ge0$. Work out an expression for $f^{-1}(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+1}$, $x\\ge-1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=x^2-1,\\quad x\\ge0\\\\x&=y^2-1,\\quad y\\ge0\\\\y^2&=x+1\\\\y&=\\sqrt{x+1}\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\sqrt{x+1},\\quad x\\ge-1\\end{align*}$$Use the nonnegative root because the restricted domain of $f$ becomes the range of $f^{-1}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q19-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Work out an expression for $g^{-1}(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{x-5}{4}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=4x+5\\\\x&=4y+5\\\\4y&=x-5\\\\y&=\\frac{x-5}{4}\\\\g^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{x-5}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q19-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Given that $fg(x)=3gf(x)$, show that $4x^2+40x+21=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$fg(x)=16x^2+40x+24$ and $gf(x)=4x^2+1$. Substituting into $fg(x)=3gf(x)$ gives $4x^2+40x+21=0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}fg(x)&=(4x+5)^2-1\\\\fg(x)&=16x^2+40x+24\\\\gf(x)&=4(x^2-1)+5\\\\gf(x)&=4x^2+1\\end{align*}$$Using $fg(x)=3gf(x)$:$$\\begin{align*}16x^2+40x+24&=3(4x^2+1)\\\\16x^2+40x+24&=12x^2+3\\\\4x^2+40x+21&=0\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
